# Technical Design: Proposed LMS Features

This document outlines the detailed architecture, database updates, API design, and frontend considerations for implementing the following features in GiteaForge:
1. **In-App Code Review** (Feature 3)
2. **Project Analytics & Progress Charts** (Feature 4)
3. **Meeting Scheduler & Discussion Boards** (Feature 5)

---

## 1. In-App Code Review

This feature lets Supervisors review Git commits and pull requests (PRs) directly within the LMS client instead of browsing the external Gitea interface.

### UI Mockups (Aligned with GiteaForge Project Detail Screen Layout)

![GiteaForge Student View: PR Status & Inline Supervisor Comments](giteaforge_student_code_review_final_1783769765109.png)

### Database Updates (`schema.prisma`)
We can add new models to support line-level code comments and PR state mappings:

```prisma
model PullRequest {
  id           String       @id @default(cuid())
  giteaPrId    Int          // The index ID of the PR on Gitea
  title        String
  description  String?
  status       String       // e.g., "OPEN", "MERGED", "CLOSED"
  projectId    String
  createdAt    DateTime     @default(now())
  updatedAt    DateTime     @updatedAt
  project      Project      @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  comments     CodeComment[]

  @@unique([projectId, giteaPrId])
  @@map("pull_requests")
}

model CodeComment {
  id            String       @id @default(cuid())
  pullRequestId String?
  commitHash    String?      // Inline comment can target a PR or a raw commit
  filePath      String
  lineNumber    Int
  content       String
  authorId      String
  createdAt     DateTime     @default(now())
  author        User         @relation(fields: [authorId], references: [id])
  pullRequest   PullRequest? @relation(fields: [pullRequestId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@map("code_comments")
}
```

### API Design
* **`GET /api/v1/projects/:id/commits/:sha/diff`**: Fetches the diff content for a commit using Gitea's comparison endpoints and returns it formatted as JSON.
* **`POST /api/v1/projects/:id/comments`**: Adds an inline code comment targeting a specific file and line number.
* **`GET /api/v1/projects/:id/comments`**: Retrieves all code comments for the project to display them inline with the code code review.

### Frontend Considerations
* **Diff Viewer**: Render file changes side-by-side or unified (using line-by-line highlight styles matching Tailwind).
* **Comment Triggers**: Add hover triggers next to diff line numbers allowing supervisors to toggle a text area and submit feedback.

