## 3. Meeting Scheduler & Discussion Boards

Provides a collaborative workspace where students and supervisors can schedule syncs, upload meeting summaries, and discuss general project details asynchronously.

### UI Mockup (Aligned with GiteaForge Project Detail Screen Layout)

![GiteaForge Meeting Scheduler & Discussion Boards: Calendar Workspace & Forums](giteaforge_meetings_final_1783769795132.png)

![meeting](image-2.png)

### Database Updates (`schema.prisma`)
Create new models for tracking schedules and forum threads:

```prisma
model Meeting {
  id            String    @id @default(cuid())
  title         String
  description   String?
  scheduledTime DateTime
  durationMins  Int       @default(30)
  meetingLink   String?
  minutesOfMeet String?   // Markdown summary logged post-meeting
  projectId     String
  createdAt     DateTime  @default(now())
  updatedAt     DateTime  @updatedAt
  project       Project   @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@map("meetings")
}

model DiscussionThread {
  id          String           @id @default(cuid())
  title       String
  projectId   String
  authorId    String
  createdAt   DateTime         @default(now())
  updatedAt   DateTime         @updatedAt
  project     Project          @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  author      User             @relation(fields: [authorId], references: [id])
  posts       DiscussionPost[]

  @@map("discussion_threads")
}

model DiscussionPost {
  id        String           @id @default(cuid())
  threadId  String
  authorId  String
  content   String
  createdAt DateTime         @default(now())
  thread    DiscussionThread @relation(fields: [threadId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  author    User             @relation(fields: [authorId], references: [id])

  @@map("discussion_posts")
}
```

### API Design
* **`POST /api/v1/projects/:id/meetings`**: Schedule a meeting and email invite.
* **`PATCH /api/v1/meetings/:id`**: Update agenda or log minutes of the meeting.
* **`GET /api/v1/projects/:id/discussions`**: Fetch discussion board threads.
* **`POST /api/v1/discussions/:threadId/posts`**: Reply to a thread.

### Frontend Considerations
* **Calendar Integration**: Provide a responsive calendar grid using clean CSS/Tailwind grid components.
* **Thread Feed**: Render post threads similar to GitHub issues, supporting markdown previews for discussion contents.

